ticket_data.description:
#36991 made `HttpRequest._set_content_type_params()` raise `BadRequest` for an invalid `Content-Type` header; before it was `LookupError`. 

**But** according to the [https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ref/exceptions/#django.core.exceptions.BadRequest docs], the behavior and intention of the change was to my understanding to get a 400 response, but current main still responds with a 500, e.g. just with

{{{
curl -i -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/ -H "Content-Type: text/plain; charset*=BOGUS''%20"
}}}

This isn't really a regression, more like an incomplete fix.

Basically the exceptions are raised when the request is created and not inside the `get_response()`, so it slips by before the aptly named `convert_exception_to_response()` is used. 

I'm intending to open a pull request shortly after this.


'Disclaimer'
I used Claude Code to investigate this bug. I saw this (super rare) error in our production env, probably coming from a security scanner. Mostly harmless, but also thought I could contribute here with a quick fix.

